WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.630
- Is it kind of an amazing thing I know

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:03.060
you've probably been
asked this a million times

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:06.740
but to be a part of
something so monumental

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:09.270
like so important and
pop culture like everyone

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.870
rushed on Thursday nights
to watch that show.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.590
Like we literally everyone
I know watched it.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:14.610
Like that's incredible-
- Yes

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.620
It's funny now I mean, it felt really huge

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.770
but the way things are
now with like social media

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.538
and streaming and your ability
to binge watch something

00:00:22.538 --> 00:00:27.130
that was back before, you
only get VCRs back then

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.167
nobody knew how to-
- You do weight

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:31.250
- Yeah but nobody could
figure out how to tape a show.

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.083
- I did.
(crowd laughing)

00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:33.500
- There're few right there
you could press record

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.520
but like to program and you got the news?

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.850
you know what i mean so but now it feels

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:44.108
somehow just as relevant
now as it did back then.

00:00:44.108 --> 00:00:44.941
- Yeah.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:47.230
- It's it's funny 'cause
we're all so much older now

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.140
You know what I mean
and you were in the TV

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.473
they look at this so
young and then he come on-

00:00:51.473 --> 00:00:53.040
- He think you look baby
- like Jesus!

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:55.530
(Everyone laughing)

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.080
- I feel like that was my career as well.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.510
Could you leave the house though back

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:01.330
in that height of it all?

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:04.120
'cause I remember we were
actually both at the same awards.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.660
I can't remember what it was
but it was during American Idol

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.330
and y'all were a couple
of y'all were there.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:11.029
And everybody was swarming around you all.

00:01:11.029 --> 00:01:14.020
And so I was like, Oh my
God, that's gotta be rough.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:15.810
- Yeah well you know
there's some weird things

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:18.225
that happened back back then.

00:01:18.225 --> 00:01:21.070
- Like what?
(crowd laughing)

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:22.382
- I remember one time,
so it was during the week

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.560
it was just like during the afternoon

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.780
I had to be flipping channels
I was watching the news

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:30.680
and for some reason, they had
like a split screen on the TV

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:35.556
six quadrants wouldn't be
quadrants, but six equal.

00:01:35.556 --> 00:01:38.610
- Six four
(everyone laughing)

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:41.670
- Each was a live shot of
each one of our houses,

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:44.677
like a helicopter shot,
they've cast of friends houses

00:01:44.677 --> 00:01:47.810
and I was like, Okay, what, what is this?

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.040
What's going on here?

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:51.200
And I'm watching it It was
like a not there was no

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:54.540
information and no news
really just showing the houses

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.750
and remember looking close at my house

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.801
and thinking (beep) I need a new roof.

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:01.350
(everyone laughing)

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:03.460
So the helicopter flies
away I get the ladder out

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.992
(mumbles)

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:07.705
- All right well man
with the plan is back.

00:02:07.705 --> 00:02:09.100
So how is this show?

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.770
How do you love the
chemistry of this cast?

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.480
- This show is fun you know,

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.490
I'd finished doing episodes for Showtime

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:16.550
which was really fun.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.654
And then, like I'd never played

00:02:18.654 --> 00:02:21.460
a guy that was in a relationship or dad

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:23.370
and you know now I have a daughter

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:26.809
and I figure I'm old now It
must be its time to play dad

00:02:26.809 --> 00:02:27.642
- [Kelly] You can play a dad
(laughing)

00:02:27.642 --> 00:02:31.610
So just, you know, sort
of high concept show.

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:32.940
It's just about this family.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.773
- Yeah.

00:02:33.773 --> 00:02:34.606
- And when you-

00:02:34.606 --> 00:02:36.300
- That's what's so relatable about it?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.460
- There's so many things that happen

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.717
just in a regular family's life

00:02:40.717 --> 00:02:42.760
that it's just been really really fun

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.380
and Stacy Keach plays my dad he's awesome.

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.900
Kevin Neon plays my brother

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.441
he's really hard to work
with because he's so funny.

00:02:49.441 --> 00:02:50.360
(laughing)

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.200
I just end up laughing all the time.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.060
Eliza Snyder plays my wife, and
we have a really great calf.

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:57.610
So we're at the season four now

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.160
and then I think it's
our best best season.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.429
- I love that it's so relatable though

00:03:02.429 --> 00:03:03.262
(crowd applauding)

00:03:03.262 --> 00:03:06.890
'cause even the scene,
even the scene we just saw

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.440
I have totally heard
our 18 year old daughter

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:13.080
and my husband just like
completely arguing about her shorts

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.804
and how they were basically
a bathing suit bottom.

00:03:15.804 --> 00:03:18.278
Yeah so it's like that
whole slow striptease thing.

00:03:18.278 --> 00:03:19.420
(laughing) so hilarious

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.800
- Yeah, my daughter 16 now
wears the same kind of thing

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.760
now where is the rest of your shirt?

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:26.279
- Why are you we have money
you can afford a whole shirt.

00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:27.646
(everyone laughing)

00:03:27.646 --> 00:03:28.746
And then you start to
think about what you did

00:03:28.746 --> 00:03:31.420
when you were younger and then
you just get frightened but-

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.870
- I didn't wear shirts like that ones.

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:34.789
(everyone laughing)

00:03:34.789 --> 00:03:37.710
- I didn't either.
(laughing)

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:40.187
I know. I'm so nervous for our girls.

